The published release carries other people's software, each under its own license:

- The machine's disk and host image (ghcr.io/christianblevens/raigolmi) are Fedora 44
  (quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44) with packages from Fedora, among them sway, foot, tmux,
  wl-clipboard, git, OpenSSH, nftables and Python. Each package's license is in its RPM
  metadata (`rpm -qi <package>` on the machine), and its source is in Fedora's source
  repositories: https://src.fedoraproject.org.
- Docker CE (docker-ce, docker-ce-cli, containerd.io, docker-buildx-plugin,
  docker-compose-plugin), installed from download.docker.com. Docker Engine, its CLI, Buildx
  and Compose, and containerd, are under the Apache License 2.0:
  https://github.com/moby/moby, https://github.com/docker/cli,
  https://github.com/docker/buildx, https://github.com/docker/compose,
  https://github.com/containerd/containerd.
- The Python packages raigolmid depends on, installed into /usr/lib/raigolmi from PyPI, each
  under the license in its own distribution metadata there.
- The machine's own container images, baked into the disk: Fedora 44 for its surfaces and
  helpers (the GitHub CLI, MIT, in one of them), and the agent image every tab runs. That one
  is Debian bookworm with Node.js 22 (node:22-bookworm-slim; Node.js is MIT), its Debian
  packages, the GitHub CLI, and Claude Code (@anthropic-ai/claude-code, the version pinned in
  agents/claude/Dockerfile). Each Debian package's license is in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright
  in the image, and its source is at https://sources.debian.org (and, for the exact version,
  https://snapshot.debian.org). Claude Code is Anthropic's, is not open source, and is used under
  Anthropic's own terms, in the LICENSE.md of its npm package; every agent in RaiGolmi is it.

The Windows app (RaiGolmi.exe) is built as one file and carries Vortice.Direct3D11,
Vortice.DXGI and Vortice.D3DCompiler with SharpGen.Runtime (MIT, Amer Koleci and
contributors: https://github.com/amerkoleci/Vortice.Windows).

`setup.bat` also installs, from their own publishers, MSYS2, the .NET 8 Desktop Runtime and
a patched QEMU (GPL-2.0) and virglrenderer (MIT) from
https://github.com/ChristianBlevens/raigolmi-packages, which holds both patches and their build
scripts; QEMU's release there carries its full source.

For the GPL-licensed software in the release, the complete corresponding source is available
from the places named above, and on request through an issue on
https://github.com/ChristianBlevens/RaiGolmi for three years from the release that carried it.
